# Without the mark the sketch is read as built; `run` writes the report to the built `Sink`, which prints it.

route archive.run
step run/Sink.new
step run/Sink.new/Sink()                                       # `Sink` is a struct built by its literal
step run/Sink.write

line entry > run call
line run/Sink.new/Sink() > Sink@run/Sink.new/Sink() value
line Sink@run/Sink.new/Sink() > run/Sink.new value             # new hands back what its body built
line run/Sink.new > Sink@run/Sink.new value
line Sink@run/Sink.new > run/Sink.write value
line run/Sink.write > Screen own

home Sink@run/Sink.new/Sink() run/Sink.new
home Sink@run/Sink.new run

side entry left
side Screen right

# building the exported Sink runs its public methods, so the literal reaches what write prints
known #74 extra line run/Sink.new/Sink() > Screen reached
